    "text": "Slow Start: > Size of the congestion window (cwnd) starts with one maximum segment size (MSS). > MSS ts determined during connection establishment by using an option of the same name. > The size of the window increases one MSS each time an ack Is received. window starts slowly, but grows exponentially. > The sender starts with cvnd =1 MSS(sender can send only one segment). After receipt of ack for segment |, size of the cwnd ts increased by I(cwnd is now 2). Now two more segments can be sent and so on.... Start =... cwnd=I Afterround 1... 9 cwnd=2! =2_ Afterround2...... cwnd=2? =4 After round 3 ..... ewnd=23 =8 > In slow-start algo, size of congestion window increases exponentially until it reaches a threshold. > In most implementations the value of ssthresh is 65,535 bytes.",
